e/docs/jobs/effort_hide-it-should-apply-to-backlog/brief.md\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":10691,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":10691},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3a7f7f0d-9cdb-4c1d-aff0-7b779c16b9eb\",\"uuid\":\"406b4a63-e322-4874-a241-4f78990c6431\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-01T15:19:47.244Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CecwkcL36FnDgDZYFfwGy\"}\n+{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_018beAq6QRnmT2Kt1ip9qjCZ\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# Brief: hide it should apply to backlog\\n2\\t\\n3\\tstatus: open\\n4\\ttype: feature\\n5\\tid: effort\\n6\\tbranch: feature/effort_hide-it-should-apply-to-backlog\\n7\\tdate: 2026-09-01\\n8\\tauthor: Leander Muskalla\\n9\\t\\n10\\t## What\\n11\\t\\n12\\tThe \\\"Hide It\\\" feature in the todo section should also apply to the backlog which right now seems to be excluded from it.\\n13\\t\\n14\\t## Why\\n15\\t\\n16\\t<!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\\n17\\t\\n18\\t## Out of scope\\n19\\t\\n20\\t<!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\\n21\\t\\n22\\t## Notes\\n23\\t\\n24\\t<!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->\\n25\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3a7f7f0d-9cdb-4c1d-aff0-7b779c16b9eb\",\"uuid\":\"ceb89b5a-01de-4f95-ac54-9ec9cec473b8\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-01T15:19:47.255Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/effort_hide-it-should-apply-to-backlog/brief.md\",\"content\":\"# Brief: hide it should apply to backlog\\n\\nstatus: open\\ntype: feature\\nid: effort\\nbranch: feature/effort_hide-it-should-apply-to-backlog\\ndate: 2026-09-01\\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\\n\\n## What\\n\\nThe \\\"Hide It\\\" feature in the todo section should also apply to the backlog which right now seems to be excluded from it.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n<!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n<!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n<!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->\\n\",\"numLines\":25,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":25}}}\n+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cecwkd9QKmgEDTbBHXjuC\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01JXYQg6o6HvPXZDDjDwovvU\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cat /workspace/docs/jobs/effort_hide-it-should-apply-to-backlog/tasks.md\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":10691,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":10691},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3a7f7f0d-9cdb-4c1d-aff0-7b779c16b9eb\",\"uuid\":\"0d947641-1de4-4c31-a99a-dbfc5aa1d61d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-01T15:19:47.514Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CecwkcL36FnDgDZYFfwGy\"}\n+{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01JXYQg6o6HvPXZDDjDwovvU\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"# Tasks: hide it should apply to backlog\\n\\nid: effort\\nstatus: open\\nanalyst: claude (analyst)\\ndate: 2026-09-01\\n\\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\\n\\n## Context / findings\\n\\nThe \\\"Hide It\\\" toggle (`src/lib/components/todos/actions/HideIt.svelte`, state in\\n`src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts`) hides todos whose category belongs to a\\nworkspace flagged `is_hideable` (`TodoFilterService.filterByHideIt`). Backlog\\nitems are normally kept out of the main todo list entirely\\n(`TodoFilterService.filterOutBacklog`, applied in `Todos.useFilters()`) and are\\nonly shown when the user explicitly picks the \\\"Backlog\\\" status filter from\\n`TodoNavigation` (`{ type: 'status', value: 'backlog' }`).\\n\\nReading `Todos.useFilters()` line by line, the hide-it filter (`filterByHideIt`)\\nis applied to `filteredTodos` regardless of which status filter is selected —\\non paper it should already apply once \\\"Backlog\\\" is selected. However, I found\\none concrete, reproducible defect in that same method that plausibly explains\\ninconsistent behaviour (including for backlog) and should be the starting\\npoint for the developer:\\n\\n- `useFilters(filters)` guards the hide-it pass with\\n  `!this.isCategoryFilterActive() && !this.isTagFilterActive()`, and those two\\n  helpers read `this.activeFilters` — but `this.activeFilters` is only updated\\n  to the new `filters` argument at the *end* of `useFilters()` (line ~201).\\n  So the hide-it guard is evaluated against the *previous* filter selection,\\n  not the one being applied. E.g.: select a category filter, then switch to\\n  the \\\"Backlog\\\" status filter — the hide-it pass sees the stale \\\"category\\n  filter active\\\" state and skips itself, so hidden-workspace backlog items\\n  leak through even though hide-it is on and no category filter is actually\\n  active anymore.\\n\\nI could **not** find a code path where hide-it is unconditionally skipped for\\nbacklog in a simple/fresh case (no prior category or tag filter) — that combo\\ntraces through `useFilters()` as working correctly. I was not able to run the\\napp or the test suite to empirically confirm the exact repro steps (no\\nexecution tooling available to this role), so TASK-1 below is a mandatory\\nreproduction step before any fix is written — do not assume the stale-filter\\ntheory is the full story until it's confirmed against the running app.\\n\\nAlso noted, likely unrelated but worth a mention: `TodoGroupingService.groupByStatus()`\\nnever creates a `backlog` group even though `KanbanView.svelte` has label/colour\\nhandling for the `'backlog'` status — so backlog items never appear on the\\nKanban board at all, independent of hide-it. Not proposing a task for this\\nsince it doesn't match \\\"Hide It should apply to backlog\\\" and would expand\\nscope; flagging so the developer doesn't confuse it with the reported bug.\\n\\n## Task breakdown\\n\\nTASK-1: Reproduce the reported bug against the running app (or by writing a\\n    failing unit test first) to pin down the exact steps under which Hide It\\n    fails to hide backlog items, confirming or ruling out the stale\\n    `this.activeFilters` read in `Todos.useFilters()` as the cause.\\n    files: none changed; investigation only (`src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts`,\\n    `src/lib/services/TodoFilterService.ts`, `tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts`)\\n    depends: none\\n    risk: low — read-only investigation, but the whole job's correctness\\n    depends on getting this right, so don't skip it.\\n\\nTASK-2: Fix `Todos.useFilters()` so the hide-it pass is evaluated against the\\n    filters actually being applied (the `filters` argument) instead of the\\n    stale `this.activeFilters`, ensuring hide-it consistently filters backlog\\n    items the same way it does every other status. Exact fix depends on\\n    TASK-1's findings — likely either reordering so `this.activeFilters =\\n    filters` happens before the hide-it guard, or having\\n    `isCategoryFilterActive`/`isTagFilterActive` take the `filters` argument\\n    directly.\\n    files: src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts\\n    depends: TASK-1\\n    risk: medium — `useFilters()` is the shared filtering path for every todo\\n    view (list, kanban, card, overview) and every filter type, so a change\\n    here has broad blast radius even though the fix itself is small.\\n\\nTASK-3: Add/extend unit test coverage for hide-it + backlog interaction in\\n    `tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts` (e.g. hide-it on, backlog status filter\\n    selected, hidden-workspace category present in a backlog todo → todo is\\n    filtered out; plus the category-filter-then-backlog-filter switch\\n    scenario from TASK-1/2) so the fix is regression-proof.\\n    files: tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts\\n    depends: TASK-2\\n    risk: low — test-only change.\\n\\n## Out of scope (per brief, left unfilled — flagging for confirmation)\\n\\n- Kanban board not rendering a \\\"Backlog\\\" column at all\\n  (`TodoGroupingService.groupByStatus`) — separate issue, not mentioned in\\n  the brief.\\n- Any change to what \\\"Hide It\\\" hides (i.e. the workspace/category-based\\n  hiding rule itself) — this job is only about making it apply consistently\\n  to the backlog status.\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3a7f7f0d-9cdb-4c1d-aff0-7b779c16b9eb\",\"uuid\":\"a928dead-c87c-45ce-915e-04089cbda737\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-01T15:19:47.552Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"# Tasks: hide it should apply to backlog\\n\\nid: effort\\nstatus: open\\nanalyst: claude (analyst)\\ndate: 2026-09-01\\n\\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\\n\\n## Context / findings\\n\\nThe \\\"Hide It\\\" toggle (`src/lib/components/todos/actions/HideIt.svelte`, state in\\n`src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts`) hides todos whose category belongs to a\\nworkspace flagged `is_hideable` (`TodoFilterService.filterByHideIt`). Backlog\\nitems are normally kept out of the main todo list entirely\\n(`TodoFilterService.filterOutBacklog`, applied in `Todos.useFilters()`) and are\\nonly shown when the user explicitly picks the \\\"Backlog\\\" status filter from\\n`TodoNavigation` (`{ type: 'status', value: 'backlog' }`).\\n\\nReading `Todos.useFilters()` line by line, the hide-it filter (`filterByHideIt`)\\nis applied to `filteredTodos` regardless of which status filter is selected —\\non paper it should already apply once \\\"Backlog\\\" is selected. However, I found\\none concrete, reproducible defect in that same method that plausibly explains\\ninconsistent behaviour (including for backlog) and should be the starting\\npoint for the developer:\\n\\n- `useFilters(filters)` guards the hide-it pass with\\n  `!this.isCategoryFilterActive() && !this.isTagFilterActive()`, and those two\\n  helpers read `this.activeFilters` — but `this.activeFilters` is only updated\\n  to the new `filters` argument at the *end* of `useFilters()` (line ~201).\\n  So the hide-it guard is evaluated against the *previous* filter selection,\\n  not the one being applied. E.g.: select a category filter, then switch to\\n  the \\\"Backlog\\\" status filter — the hide-it pass sees the stale \\\"category\\n  filter active\\\" state and skips itself, so hidden-workspace backlog items\\n  leak through even though hide-it is on and no category filter is actually\\n  active anymore.\\n\\nI could **not** find a code path where hide-it is unconditionally skipped for\\nbacklog in a simple/fresh case (no prior category or tag filter) — that combo\\ntraces through `useFilters()` as working correctly. I was not able to run the\\napp or the test suite to empirically confirm the exact repro steps (no\\nexecution tooling available to this role), so TASK-1 below is a mandatory\\nreproduction step before any fix is written — do not assume the stale-filter\\ntheory is the full story until it's confirmed against the running app.\\n\\nAlso noted, likely unrelated but worth a mention: `TodoGroupingService.groupByStatus()`\\nnever creates a `backlog` group even though `KanbanView.svelte` has label/colour\\nhandling for the `'backlog'` status — so backlog items never appear on the\\nKanban board at all, independent of hide-it. Not proposing a task for this\\nsince it doesn't match \\\"Hide It should apply to backlog\\\" and would expand\\nscope; flagging so the developer doesn't confuse it with the reported bug.\\n\\n## Task breakdown\\n\\nTASK-1: Reproduce the reported bug against the running app (or by writing a\\n    failing unit test first) to pin down the exact steps under which Hide It\\n    fails to hide backlog items, confirming or ruling out the stale\\n    `this.activeFilters` read in `Todos.useFilters()` as the cause.\\n    files: none changed; investigation only (`src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts`,\\n    `src/lib/services/TodoFilterService.ts`, `tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts`)\\n    depends: none\\n    risk: low — read-only investigation, but the whole job's correctness\\n    depends on getting this right, so don't skip it.\\n\\nTASK-2: Fix `Todos.useFilters()` so the hide-it pass is evaluated against the\\n    filters actually being applied (the `filters` argument) instead of the\\n    stale `this.activeFilters`, ensuring hide-it consistently filters backlog\\n    items the same way it does every other status. Exact fix depends on\\n    TASK-1's findings — likely either reordering so `this.activeFilters =\\n    filters` happens before the hide-it guard, or having\\n    `isCategoryFilterActive`/`isTagFilterActive` take the `filters` argument\\n    directly.\\n    files: src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts\\n    depends: TASK-1\\n    risk: medium — `useFilters()` is the shared filtering path for every todo\\n    view (list, kanban, card, overview) and every filter type, so a change\\n    here has broad blast radius even though the fix itself is small.\\n\\nTASK-3: Add/extend unit test coverage for hide-it + backlog interaction in\\n    `tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts` (e.g. hide-it on, backlog status filter\\n    selected, hidden-workspace category present in a backlog todo → todo is\\n    filtered out; plus the category-filter-then-backlog-filter switch\\n    scenario from TASK-1/2) so the fix is regression-proof.\\n    files: tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts\\n    depends: TASK-2\\n    risk: low — test-only change.\\n\\n## Out of scope (per brief, left unfilled — flagging for confirmation)\\n\\n- Kanban board not rendering a \\\"Backlog\\\" column at all\\n  (`TodoGroupingService.groupByStatus`) — separate issue, not mentioned in\\n  the brief.\\n- Any change to what \\\"Hide It\\\" hides (i.e. the workspace/category-based\\n  hiding rule itself) — this job is only about making it apply consistently\\n  to the backlog status.\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}\n+{\"type\":\"rate_limit_event\",\"rate_limit_info\":{\"status\":\"allowed\",\"resetsAt\":1788285600,\"rateLimitType\":\"five_hour\",\"overageStatus\":\"rejected\",\"overageDisabledReason\":\"org_level_disabled\",\"isUsingOverage\":false,\"unifiedWindows\":{\"five_hour\":{\"utilization\":0.65,\"resetsAt\":1788285600},\"seven_day\":{\"utilization\":0.19,\"resetsAt\":1788663600}}},\"uuid\":\"4fcd6ef3-da44-48a3-8af9-b2bbbc633819\",\"session_id\":\"3a7f7f0d-9cdb-4c1d-aff0-7b779c16b9eb\"}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a7f7f0d-9cdb-4c1d-aff0-7b779c16b9eb","uuid":"0b8b9b99-3cb0-47e5-ac00-a50f1fa433e7","timestamp":"2026-09-01T15:21:11.694Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/docs/jobs/effort_hide-it-should-apply-to-backlog/session.log b/docs/jobs/effort_hide-it-should-apply-to-backlog/session.log\nindex f6d3034..50ea720 100644\n--- a/docs/jobs/effort_hide-it-should-apply-to-backlog/session.log\n+++ b/docs/jobs/effort_hide-it-should-apply-to-backlog/session.log\n@@ -329,3 +329,106 @@\n {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cecwjwds6Q6wxpLr5hHch\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I've completed the analysis and written the task breakdown to `docs/jobs/effort_hide-it-should-apply-to-backlog/tasks.md`. Summary:\\n\\n**Branch check:** confirmed the worktree is on `feature/effort_hide-it-should-apply-to-backlog`, matching `brief.md`.\\n\\n**Findings:** I traced the \\\"Hide It\\\" logic (`Todos.svelte.ts` → `useFilters()`, `TodoFilterService.filterByHideIt`/`filterOutBacklog`). On paper, hide-it already applies to the backlog view in the simple case — but I found one concrete, reproducible defect: `useFilters()` checks `isCategoryFilterActive()`/`isTagFilterActive()` against `this.activeFilters`, which is only updated to the new filter selection at the *end* of the function — so the hide-it guard can evaluate against the *previous* filter state (e.g. switching from a category filter to the \\\"Backlog\\\" status filter). I could not find a path where hide-it is unconditionally skipped for backlog in the simplest case, and I have no way to run the app or test suite from this role to confirm empirically.\\n\\n**Tasks produced:**\\n- TASK-1 (low risk): mandatory reproduction step before any fix, to confirm or rule out the stale-filter theory.\\n- TASK-2 (medium risk): fix `Todos.useFilters()` in `src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts`, depends on TASK-1.\\n- TASK-3 (low risk): add regression tests in `tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts`, depends on TASK-2.\\n\\nI flagged a separate, likely-unrelated observation (Kanban board never shows a backlog column) as out-of-scope rather than turning it into a task, since it doesn't match the brief and would expand scope unnecessarily.\\n\\nI did not modify `brief.md`, `implementation.md`, or `verdict.md` — those are template placeholders owned by other roles (product/developer/reviewer) and out of scope for the analyst step.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2311,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":93224,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2311},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\