{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E7kCeGuLHM9cpT8bzFTBkH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tasks: hide it should apply to backlog\n2\t\n3\tid: effort\n4\tstatus: open\n5\tanalyst: claude (analyst)\n6\tdate: 2026-09-01\n7\t\n8\t<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n9\t\n10\t## Context / findings\n11\t\n12\tThe \"Hide It\" toggle (`src/lib/components/todos/actions/HideIt.svelte`, state in\n13\t`src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts`) hides todos whose category belongs to a\n14\tworkspace flagged `is_hideable` (`TodoFilterService.filterByHideIt`). Backlog\n15\titems are normally kept out of the main todo list entirely\n16\t(`TodoFilterService.filterOutBacklog`, applied in `Todos.useFilters()`) and are\n17\tonly shown when the user explicitly picks the \"Backlog\" status filter from\n18\t`TodoNavigation` (`{ type: 'status', value: 'backlog' }`).\n19\t\n20\tReading `Todos.useFilters()` line by line, the hide-it filter (`filterByHideIt`)\n21\tis applied to `filteredTodos` regardless of which status filter is selected —\n22\ton paper it should already apply once \"Backlog\" is selected. However, I found\n23\tone concrete, reproducible defect in that same method that plausibly explains\n24\tinconsistent behaviour (including for backlog) and should be the starting\n25\tpoint for the developer:\n26\t\n27\t- `useFilters(filters)` guards the hide-it pass with\n28\t  `!this.isCategoryFilterActive() && !this.isTagFilterActive()`, and those two\n29\t  helpers read `this.activeFilters` — but `this.activeFilters` is only updated\n30\t  to the new `filters` argument at the *end* of `useFilters()` (line ~201).\n31\t  So the hide-it guard is evaluated against the *previous* filter selection,\n32\t  not the one being applied. E.g.: select a category filter, then switch to\n33\t  the \"Backlog\" status filter — the hide-it pass sees the stale \"category\n34\t  filter active\" state and skips itself, so hidden-workspace backlog items\n35\t  leak through even though hide-it is on and no category filter is actually\n36\t  active anymore.\n37\t\n38\tI could **not** find a code path where hide-it is unconditionally skipped for\n39\tbacklog in a simple/fresh case (no prior category or tag filter) — that combo\n40\ttraces through `useFilters()` as working correctly. I was not able to run the\n41\tapp or the test suite to empirically confirm the exact repro steps (no\n42\texecution tooling available to this role), so TASK-1 below is a mandatory\n43\treproduction step before any fix is written — do not assume the stale-filter\n44\ttheory is the full story until it's confirmed against the running app.\n45\t\n46\tAlso noted, likely unrelated but worth a mention: `TodoGroupingService.groupByStatus()`\n47\tnever creates a `backlog` group even though `KanbanView.svelte` has label/colour\n48\thandling for the `'backlog'` status — so backlog items never appear on the\n49\tKanban board at all, independent of hide-it. Not proposing a task for this\n50\tsince it doesn't match \"Hide It should apply to backlog\" and would expand\n51\tscope; flagging so the developer doesn't confuse it with the reported bug.\n52\t\n53\t## Task breakdown\n54\t\n55\tTASK-1: Reproduce the reported bug against the running app (or by writing a\n56\t    failing unit test first) to pin down the exact steps under which Hide It\n57\t    fails to hide backlog items, confirming or ruling out the stale\n58\t    `this.activeFilters` read in `Todos.useFilters()` as the cause.\n59\t    files: none changed; investigation only (`src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts`,\n60\t    `src/lib/services/TodoFilterService.ts`, `tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts`)\n61\t    depends: none\n62\t    risk: low — read-only investigation, but the whole job's correctness\n63\t    depends on getting this right, so don't skip it.\n64\t\n65\tTASK-2: Fix `Todos.useFilters()` so the hide-it pass is evaluated against the\n66\t    filters actually being applied (the `filters` argument) instead of the\n67\t    stale `this.activeFilters`, ensuring hide-it consistently filters backlog\n68\t    items the same way it does every other status. Exact fix depends on\n69\t    TASK-1's findings — likely either reordering so `this.activeFilters =\n70\t    filters` happens before the hide-it guard, or having\n71\t    `isCategoryFilterActive`/`isTagFilterActive` take the `filters` argument\n72\t    directly.\n73\t    files: src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts\n74\t    depends: TASK-1\n75\t    risk: medium — `useFilters()` is the shared filtering path for every todo\n76\t    view (list, kanban, card, overview) and every filter type, so a change\n77\t    here has broad blast radius even though the fix itself is small.\n78\t\n79\tTASK-3: Add/extend unit test coverage for hide-it + backlog interaction in\n80\t    `tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts` (e.g. hide-it on, backlog status filter\n81\t    selected, hidden-workspace category present in a backlog todo → todo is\n82\t    filtered out; plus the category-filter-then-backlog-filter switch\n83\t    scenario from TASK-1/2) so the fix is regression-proof.\n84\t    files: tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts\n85\t    depends: TASK-2\n86\t    risk: low — test-only change.\n87\t\n88\t## Out of scope (per brief, left unfilled — flagging for confirmation)\n89\t\n90\t- Kanban board not rendering a \"Backlog\" column at all\n91\t  (`TodoGroupingService.groupByStatus`) — separate issue, not mentioned in\n92\t  the brief.\n93\t- Any change to what \"Hide It\" hides (i.e. the workspace/category-based\n94\t  hiding rule itself) — this job is only about making it apply consistently\n95\t  to the backlog status.\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f3f90b9-b7a3-4052-9957-ecf5ab16ce8c","uuid":"2cfd831c-c130-4e60-94bf-9eb017ee8ec3","timestamp":"2026-09-01T15:22:15.748Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/effort_hide-it-should-apply-to-backlog/tasks.md","content":"# Tasks: hide it should apply to backlog\n\nid: effort\nstatus: open\nanalyst: claude (analyst)\ndate: 2026-09-01\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context / findings\n\nThe \"Hide It\" toggle (`src/lib/components/todos/actions/HideIt.svelte`, state in\n`src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts`) hides todos whose category belongs to a\nworkspace flagged `is_hideable` (`TodoFilterService.filterByHideIt`). Backlog\nitems are normally kept out of the main todo list entirely\n(`TodoFilterService.filterOutBacklog`, applied in `Todos.useFilters()`) and are\nonly shown when the user explicitly picks the \"Backlog\" status filter from\n`TodoNavigation` (`{ type: 'status', value: 'backlog' }`).\n\nReading `Todos.useFilters()` line by line, the hide-it filter (`filterByHideIt`)\nis applied to `filteredTodos` regardless of which status filter is selected —\non paper it should already apply once \"Backlog\" is selected. However, I found\none concrete, reproducible defect in that same method that plausibly explains\ninconsistent behaviour (including for backlog) and should be the starting\npoint for the developer:\n\n- `useFilters(filters)` guards the hide-it pass with\n  `!this.isCategoryFilterActive() && !this.isTagFilterActive()`, and those two\n  helpers read `this.activeFilters` — but `this.activeFilters` is only updated\n  to the new `filters` argument at the *end* of `useFilters()` (line ~201).\n  So the hide-it guard is evaluated against the *previous* filter selection,\n  not the one being applied. E.g.: select a category filter, then switch to\n  the \"Backlog\" status filter — the hide-it pass sees the stale \"category\n  filter active\" state and skips itself, so hidden-workspace backlog items\n  leak through even though hide-it is on and no category filter is actually\n  active anymore.\n\nI could **not** find a code path where hide-it is unconditionally skipped for\nbacklog in a simple/fresh case (no prior category or tag filter) — that combo\ntraces through `useFilters()` as working correctly. I was not able to run the\napp or the test suite to empirically confirm the exact repro steps (no\nexecution tooling available to this role), so TASK-1 below is a mandatory\nreproduction step before any fix is written — do not assume the stale-filter\ntheory is the full story until it's confirmed against the running app.\n\nAlso noted, likely unrelated but worth a mention: `TodoGroupingService.groupByStatus()`\nnever creates a `backlog` group even though `KanbanView.svelte` has label/colour\nhandling for the `'backlog'` status — so backlog items never appear on the\nKanban board at all, independent of hide-it. Not proposing a task for this\nsince it doesn't match \"Hide It should apply to backlog\" and would expand\nscope; flagging so the developer doesn't confuse it with the reported bug.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Reproduce the reported bug against the running app (or by writing a\n    failing unit test first) to pin down the exact steps under which Hide It\n    fails to hide backlog items, confirming or ruling out the stale\n    `this.activeFilters` read in `Todos.useFilters()` as the cause.\n    files: none changed; investigation only (`src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts`,\n    `src/lib/services/TodoFilterService.ts`, `tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts`)\n    depends: none\n    risk: low — read-only investigation, but the whole job's correctness\n    depends on getting this right, so don't skip it.\n\nTASK-2: Fix `Todos.useFilters()` so the hide-it pass is evaluated against the\n    filters actually being applied (the `filters` argument) instead of the\n    stale `this.activeFilters`, ensuring hide-it consistently filters backlog\n    items the same way it does every other status. Exact fix depends on\n    TASK-1's findings — likely either reordering so `this.activeFilters =\n    filters` happens before the hide-it guard, or having\n    `isCategoryFilterActive`/`isTagFilterActive` take the `filters` argument\n    directly.\n    files: src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts\n    depends: TASK-1\n    risk: medium — `useFilters()` is the shared filtering path for every todo\n    view (list, kanban, card, overview) and every filter type, so a change\n    here has broad blast radius even though the fix itself is small.\n\nTASK-3: Add/extend unit test coverage for hide-it + backlog interaction in\n    `tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts` (e.g. hide-it on, backlog status filter\n    selected, hidden-workspace category present in a backlog todo → todo is\n    filtered out; plus the category-filter-then-backlog-filter switch\n    scenario from TASK-1/2) so the fix is regression-proof.\n    files: tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts\n    depends: TASK-2\n    risk: low — test-only change.\n\n## Out of scope (per brief, left unfilled — flagging for confirmation)\n\n- Kanban board not rendering a \"Backlog\" column at all\n  (`TodoGroupingService.groupByStatus`) — separate issue, not mentioned in\n  the brief.\n- Any change to what \"Hide It\" hides (i.e. the workspace/category-based\n  hiding rule itself) — this job is only about making it apply consistently\n  to the backlog status.\n","numLines":96,"startLine":1,"totalLines":96}}}
