{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WYQiuji7oFvs8JwV7q6xNi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## Summary\n2\t\n3\tFixed a bug where the \"Hide It\" toggle stopped filtering hidden-workspace\n4\ttodos out of the list after the user switched filters — most visibly when\n5\tswitching from a category filter to the \"Backlog\" status filter, which let\n6\tbacklog items from hideable workspaces leak through even with Hide It on.\n7\t\n8\t## Changes\n9\t\n10\tTASK-1: Reproduced the bug via a temporary unit test (not committed) before\n11\ttouching any source, per the task's mandatory-repro requirement. Confirmed\n12\tthe analyst's theory: `Todos.useFilters()` guards the hide-it pass with\n13\t`isCategoryFilterActive()`/`isTagFilterActive()`, which read\n14\t`this.activeFilters` — but `this.activeFilters` was only reassigned to the\n15\tnew `filters` argument at the *end* of `useFilters()`. So the guard evaluated\n16\tagainst the previous filter selection. Reproduced with: select a category\n17\tfilter, then switch to the backlog status filter — hide-it wrongly skipped\n18\titself because it still saw the stale \"category filter active\" state.\n19\t\n20\tTASK-2: `src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts` — moved `this.activeFilters =\n21\tfilters;` to the top of `useFilters()`, before the hide-it guard, instead of\n22\tat the end. The guard (`isCategoryFilterActive()`/`isTagFilterActive()`) now\n23\talways reflects the filters actually being applied in the current call, so\n24\thide-it consistently applies to backlog (and every other status) regardless\n25\tof what was selected before.\n26\t\n27\tTASK-3: `tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts` — added two regression tests: (1)\n28\thide-it hides hidden-workspace backlog todos when the backlog status filter\n29\tis selected fresh, (2) hide-it still hides them after switching from a\n30\tcategory filter to the backlog filter (the exact repro from TASK-1).\n31\t\n32\t## Known issues / follow-ups\n33\t\n34\t- Two pre-existing, unrelated test failures observed in the full `vitest run`\n35\t  (not caused by this change, files untouched by it):\n36\t  `tests/unit/services/TodoFilterService.test.ts` (\"keeps only todos due\n37\t  within the current week\" — date-boundary flakiness tied to today's date)\n38\t  and `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts` (\"StatisticWidget applies the\n39\t  requested color classes\"). Both are out of scope for this job.\n40\t- Per the analyst's notes, `TodoGroupingService.groupByStatus()` never\n41\t  creates a `backlog` group, so backlog items never show on the Kanban\n42\t  board — unrelated to Hide It and left out of scope as flagged in\n43\t  `tasks.md`.\n44\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f3f90b9-b7a3-4052-9957-ecf5ab16ce8c","uuid":"9e96a02c-3ade-402d-bdb9-cdfceb25c4b0","timestamp":"2026-09-01T15:22:16.273Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/effort_hide-it-should-apply-to-backlog/implementation.md","content":"## Summary\n\nFixed a bug where the \"Hide It\" toggle stopped filtering hidden-workspace\ntodos out of the list after the user switched filters — most visibly when\nswitching from a category filter to the \"Backlog\" status filter, which let\nbacklog items from hideable workspaces leak through even with Hide It on.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: Reproduced the bug via a temporary unit test (not committed) before\ntouching any source, per the task's mandatory-repro requirement. Confirmed\nthe analyst's theory: `Todos.useFilters()` guards the hide-it pass with\n`isCategoryFilterActive()`/`isTagFilterActive()`, which read\n`this.activeFilters` — but `this.activeFilters` was only reassigned to the\nnew `filters` argument at the *end* of `useFilters()`. So the guard evaluated\nagainst the previous filter selection. Reproduced with: select a category\nfilter, then switch to the backlog status filter — hide-it wrongly skipped\nitself because it still saw the stale \"category filter active\" state.\n\nTASK-2: `src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts` — moved `this.activeFilters =\nfilters;` to the top of `useFilters()`, before the hide-it guard, instead of\nat the end. The guard (`isCategoryFilterActive()`/`isTagFilterActive()`) now\nalways reflects the filters actually being applied in the current call, so\nhide-it consistently applies to backlog (and every other status) regardless\nof what was selected before.\n\nTASK-3: `tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts` — added two regression tests: (1)\nhide-it hides hidden-workspace backlog todos when the backlog status filter\nis selected fresh, (2) hide-it still hides them after switching from a\ncategory filter to the backlog filter (the exact repro from TASK-1).\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- Two pre-existing, unrelated test failures observed in the full `vitest run`\n  (not caused by this change, files untouched by it):\n  `tests/unit/services/TodoFilterService.test.ts` (\"keeps only todos due\n  within the current week\" — date-boundary flakiness tied to today's date)\n  and `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts` (\"StatisticWidget applies the\n  requested color classes\"). Both are out of scope for this job.\n- Per the analyst's notes, `TodoGroupingService.groupByStatus()` never\n  creates a `backlog` group, so backlog items never show on the Kanban\n  board — unrelated to Hide It and left out of scope as flagged in\n  `tasks.md`.\n","numLines":44,"startLine":1,"totalLines":44}}}
